    ### 2. Systemd User Services
    
    You need to create these files in `~/.config/systemd/user/`.
    
    **File 1: `~/.config/systemd/user/jellyfin-wallpaper-tracker.service`**
    ```ini
    [Unit]
    Description=Jellyfin Wallpaper Lock Tracker
    
    [Service]
    ExecStart=%h/Scripts-Apps-Plugins/Scripts/lock-screen.bash --track
    Restart=always
    
    [Install]
    WantedBy=default.target
    ```
    
    **File 2: `~/.config/systemd/user/jellyfin-wallpaper-sync.service`**
    ```ini
    [Unit]
    Description=Jellyfin Wallpaper Sync
    
    [Service]
    ExecStart=%h/Scripts-Apps-Plugins/Scripts/lock-screen.bash --sync
    
    [Install]
    WantedBy=default.target
    ```
    
    **File 3: `~/.config/systemd/user/jellyfin-wallpaper-sync.timer`**
    ```ini
    [Unit]
    Description=Run Jellyfin Wallpaper Sync every 15 minutes
    
    [Timer]
    OnBootSec=5min
    OnUnitActiveSec=15min
    
    [Install]
    WantedBy=timers.target
    ```
    
    ---
    
    ### 3. Final Activation Commands
    
    Once you have created the files, run these commands in your terminal:
    
    ```bash
    # 1. Reload systemd to see new files
    systemctl --user daemon-reload
    
    # 2. Enable and start the tracker (runs in background)
    systemctl --user enable --now jellyfin-wallpaper-tracker.service
    
    # 3. Enable and start the timer (runs the sync periodically)
    systemctl --user enable --now jellyfin-wallpaper-sync.timer
    
    # 4. Make the script executable
    chmod +x ~/Scripts-Apps-Plugins/Scripts/lock-screen.bash
    ```
    
